KNOWNBUG libstdcxx16 libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ duration: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body
--
With the libstdc++ 16.2.0 headers (g++ 16.2.0), <chrono> lost the body of
`__get_leap_second_info': its local `constexpr leap_second_info
__after_last{.is_leap_second = false, .elapsed = seconds(...)}' passed
the designated-initializer node to seconds' constructor.  Fixed with
cpp20_designated_initializer_of_class_type_member.  Runs only with GCC 16
headers (libstdcxx16).
